  "name": "Lüju (Shandong opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Shandong regional opera that grew in the early twentieth century in the Guangrao and Boxing area of the Yellow River delta, when performers of Shandong qinshu narrative singing began to act out their stories in costume; it later centred on Jinan and entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2008. Its lead instrument is the zhuiqin bowed lute (the zhuihu card in its qinshu setting), joined by yangqin, sanxian, pipa and erhu.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2000s lüju, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. zhuihu, traditional bamboo yangqin, sanxian, pipa, bamboo stick horsehair threaded between strings erhu. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
